{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2019-259", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/259", "wordCount": 1874, "segments": [{"start": 12.0, "text": "Hi. My name is Alex Schaefer,"}, {"start": 13.0, "text": "and I'm an engineer on the iOS"}, {"start": 15.0, "text": "system UI team."}, {"start": 16.0, "text": "And this is Targeting Content"}, {"start": 17.0, "text": "with Multiple Windows."}, {"start": 18.0, "text": "To get a sense of the problem"}, {"start": 19.0, "text": "we're going to talk about today,"}, {"start": 21.0, "text": "let's take a quick detour to iOS"}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "12."}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "In iOS 12, we had a 1-to-1"}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "mapping between your application"}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "and your user interface."}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "Let's say a notification comes"}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "in."}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "The user taps on it."}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "It gets routed to your app, and"}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "your app will update your user"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "interface in response."}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "Great. What could be different?"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "Well, in iOS 13, you could have"}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "multiple user interfaces running"}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "which raises the question -"}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "Which scene should activate in"}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "response to this notification?"}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "Well, I know what you're all saying."}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "Just ask my app."}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "Well, I guess."}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "But what if your app isn't"}, {"start": 58.0, "text": "running?"}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "Who cares?"}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "Just launch my app."}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "Well, hold your horses."}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "iOS needs to know which scene in"}, {"start": 66.0, "text": "your application should be"}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "frontmost and activated in"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "response to that launch event,"}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "like that incoming notification."}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "So, if we're going to background"}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "launch your app and ask for the"}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "appropriate scene, we'd have to"}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "wait until your app is fully"}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "loaded and then wait again until"}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "you could've made that"}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "determination."}, {"start": 81.0, "text": "This could lead to a"}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "less-than-desirable user"}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "experience."}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "The system would basically grind"}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "to a halt waiting for that"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "feedback."}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "And when I tap a notification, I"}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "expect it to go somewhere"}, {"start": 89.0, "text": "immediately."}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "So, what could we do about that?"}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "Well, let's take a step back and"}, {"start": 95.0, "text": "let's think about what we have"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "to work with with the system."}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "We have your application."}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "Maybe it's running, maybe it"}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "isn't."}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "Your app has your scenes and"}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "also the knowledge of the"}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "capabilities of each scene."}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "That's going to come in handy."}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "And finally, the system has this"}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "incoming notification."}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "We've talked about why we can't"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "rely on activating your app, and"}, {"start": 118.0, "text": "we know that the notification"}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "has to somehow trigger an"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "appropriate scene to be"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "activated."}, {"start": 123.0, "text": "So, let's try and pull together"}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "a solution, given these"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "constraints."}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "First, we need to find a way to"}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "describe what that notification"}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "pertains to."}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "So, let's add some of the"}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "notification that lets the"}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "system know what it is about."}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "Then we need to get your scenes"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "to describe somehow something"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "about their capabilities."}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "You know, what kind of content"}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "they can show."}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "Well, if your scenes are"}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "describing what kind of content"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "they can work with to the"}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "system, and the notification has"}, {"start": 151.0, "text": "this hint about what it's about,"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "then we don't really need your"}, {"start": 155.0, "text": "app."}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "The system is informed enough to"}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "make a selection of a desired"}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "scene to activate in response to"}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "this notification."}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "So, to think about that and"}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "think about those capabilities,"}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "we need to think about what's,"}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "what those capabilities are."}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "And those capabilities are"}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "housed within this UIKit class,"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "UI Scene Activation Conditions."}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "This is an object attached to"}, {"start": 180.0, "text": "UIScene."}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "And your scene activation"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "conditions are really just a"}, {"start": 183.0, "text": "couple of NS predicates that set"}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "the course for what specific"}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "scene can activate for it."}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "Let's dig into the API."}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "So, your activation condition"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "consists of two parts, your"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "canned predicate and your preferred predicate."}, {"start": 199.0, "text": "You should think of the canned"}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "predicate as the main predicate"}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "of the two."}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "This is expressing to the system"}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "what kind of content the scene"}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "can display."}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "Your prefers predicate is a way"}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "to express to the system that"}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "this scene is especially"}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "interested in a particular type"}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "of content."}, {"start": 215.0, "text": "You should think of canned as"}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "expressing capability and prefer"}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "is a way to delineate amongst"}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "the capable scenes the content"}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "that should be chosen."}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "I've told you these predicates"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "help you define your"}, {"start": 225.0, "text": "capabilities, but I haven't"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "really gone into detail about"}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "what these predicates operate"}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "on."}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "These predicates operate on"}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "something called target content"}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "identifiers."}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "You might be asking yourself"}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "what that is."}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "Target content identifier is a"}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "string."}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "It's just the string."}, {"start": 241.0, "text": "But, it's a little bit more"}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "complicated than that."}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "A target content identifier is a"}, {"start": 245.0, "text": "structured way to represent data"}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "within your model."}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "The system's not going to access"}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "your model - that's your job."}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "But what we're going to use that"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "for is a way to build off these"}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "scene activation conditions."}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "iOS 13 is going to use that"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "target content identifier and"}, {"start": 260.0, "text": "evaluate it against your scene"}, {"start": 262.0, "text": "activation conditions for all"}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "the scenes your application has"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "and use it that to make the call"}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "on what scene the content should"}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "be targeted to."}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "Clown Town is our exciting demo"}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "application which answers the"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "age old question - What would it"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "be like to order a clown at any"}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "time to my current location?"}, {"start": 277.0, "text": "So, let's take a look at what a"}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "target content identifier might"}, {"start": 283.0, "text": "look like for Clown Town."}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "So, this looks exactly like a"}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "URL. In this case, Clown Town is"}, {"start": 289.0, "text": "actually using a universal link."}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "Like we were saying, target"}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "content identifiers should"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "ideally express in a structured"}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "format, just like a universal"}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "link or URL."}, {"start": 298.0, "text": "Many of you are already using a"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "universal link and that'll be"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "great here as your target"}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "content identifier."}, {"start": 305.0, "text": "Let's take a look where in the"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "SDK target content identifiers"}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "have been added."}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "First, UNNotification Content."}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "New in iOS 13, you can actually"}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "augment your JSON payload prior"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "to sending it off to the Apple"}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "Push notification server with a"}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "new key, Target Content ID."}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "So, this raises also a very"}, {"start": 325.0, "text": "important point. You can actually structure this"}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "target content identifier the"}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "same on your back-end server and"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "actually pinpoint what scene"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "that notification should open up"}, {"start": 334.0, "text": "in."}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "Next, UI application shortcut"}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "item has been extended to allow"}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "for using target content"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "identifiers."}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "New in iPad OS this year, you"}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "can actually long press on an"}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "icon in the homescreen and get"}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "the same quick actions you've"}, {"start": 346.0, "text": "been using on your iPhone."}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "And finally, NS user activity."}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "Use this date restoration as"}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "well as features like handoff"}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "could also be very useful there."}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "So, let's set up that scene in"}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "Clown Town in response to that"}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "target content identifier we"}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "just talked about."}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "Up top we have our target"}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "content identifier."}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "It's our URL format and it looks"}, {"start": 371.0, "text": "like it's geared towards a clown"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "named Crusty."}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "Okay."}, {"start": 375.0, "text": "On your left, we have a general"}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "overview of all clowns we can"}, {"start": 378.0, "text": "order in the area."}, {"start": 380.0, "text": "This is our main scene and where"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "all content in our application"}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "lives."}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "The user's really unlikely to"}, {"start": 386.0, "text": "associate Crusty with this"}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "scene."}, {"start": 388.0, "text": "I think it would be ideal to set"}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "this scene's activation"}, {"start": 390.0, "text": "conditions up in such a way that"}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "it can display anything but"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "doesn't prefer anything"}, {"start": 395.0, "text": "specifically. And that makes sense."}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "It's my main scene and where I"}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "enter into my application, it"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "has all my content."}, {"start": 401.0, "text": "Lucky for us, that's actually"}, {"start": 403.0, "text": "the default when you create a"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "new scene."}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "Your UIScene Activation"}, {"start": 406.0, "text": "conditions will be set up to"}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "allow any content, or can allow"}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "any content, but not prefer"}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "anything specifically."}, {"start": 414.0, "text": "Alright."}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "On your right, we have a scene"}, {"start": 418.0, "text": "set up just for Crusty."}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "This scene can display any"}, {"start": 424.0, "text": "specific clown's details but"}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "it's likely the user would"}, {"start": 427.0, "text": "associate Crusty with this scene"}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "specifically."}, {"start": 429.0, "text": "So, we should express that"}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "association within our scene"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "activation conditions, as the"}, {"start": 436.0, "text": "scene can be activated, and we"}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "prefer it to be activated"}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "specifically for Crusty."}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "So, let's take these"}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "requirements and put together"}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "some scene activation conditions"}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "for our Detail scene."}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "Okay, let's break this down."}, {"start": 450.0, "text": "For this scene, we want to only"}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "activate if this scene is about"}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "Crusty. And so we're just going to check"}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "to see if the target content"}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "identifier that's passed in is"}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "equal to the one we would expect"}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "for Crusty."}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "Cool."}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "Now, you'll note that this is a"}, {"start": 464.0, "text": "place where we actually use the"}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "same predicate for our can and"}, {"start": 467.0, "text": "our prefers."}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "This is a pretty common pattern"}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "you'll find yourself using when"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "you want to target a scene for a"}, {"start": 472.0, "text": "specific piece of content."}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "Sure, we could accept any other"}, {"start": 476.0, "text": "clown here. It's just a detail scene."}, {"start": 478.0, "text": "But if I have a notification"}, {"start": 480.0, "text": "come in, I want it to be"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "targeted to exactly where Crusty"}, {"start": 482.0, "text": "is."}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "Cool. So, let's talk about what"}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "happens when we set these"}, {"start": 489.0, "text": "predicates."}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "When I set the Crusty predicate"}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "on our scene activation"}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "condition, the system's going to"}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "package these predicates up and"}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "ship them off to somewhere else"}, {"start": 497.0, "text": "in the operating system."}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "That has a couple repercussions"}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "for how NSPredicate is used"}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "within scene activation"}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "conditions and I'd like to go"}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "over them right now."}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "Scene activation conditions have"}, {"start": 509.0, "text": "three restrictions with its use"}, {"start": 511.0, "text": "of NSPredicate."}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "First, block-based predicates"}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "aren't allowed."}, {"start": 516.0, "text": "Unfortunately, we can't package"}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "up code within your running"}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "application and ship it out to"}, {"start": 521.0, "text": "other parts of the system."}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "Next, regular expression-based"}, {"start": 526.0, "text": "predicates aren't allowed."}, {"start": 528.0, "text": "We can't use them because they"}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "could introduce an indeterminate"}, {"start": 530.0, "text": "amount of time during the"}, {"start": 531.0, "text": "evaluation of your scene"}, {"start": 533.0, "text": "predicates."}, {"start": 535.0, "text": "We encourage you to take a look at the like operator."}, {"start": 536.0, "text": "It's the de facto glob operator"}, {"start": 538.0, "text": "to NSPredicate and it should"}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "help you do all the kinds of wildcard matching you might want"}, {"start": 542.0, "text": "to do."}, {"start": 543.0, "text": "With that being said, if you"}, {"start": 545.0, "text": "have a unique thought on how you"}, {"start": 547.0, "text": "might use a regular expression"}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "predicate, please use the"}, {"start": 550.0, "text": "feedback assistant and inform us"}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "of what you're thinking."}, {"start": 552.0, "text": "We'd really like to hear about"}, {"start": 553.0, "text": "it."}, {"start": 555.0, "text": "And finally, the only keypath"}, {"start": 557.0, "text": "your NSPredicate can reference"}, {"start": 558.0, "text": "is self."}, {"start": 560.0, "text": "Which is to say, you're not"}, {"start": 561.0, "text": "going to set your scene"}, {"start": 563.0, "text": "activation requirement"}, {"start": 564.0, "text": "predicates on something along"}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "the lines of the length of the"}, {"start": 567.0, "text": "string or your target content"}, {"start": 569.0, "text": "identifier."}, {"start": 570.0, "text": "We want you to put real content"}, {"start": 572.0, "text": "that you could actually use in your model there."}, {"start": 574.0, "text": "Next, let's take a look at"}, {"start": 577.0, "text": "another example for what their"}, {"start": 578.0, "text": "scene activation conditions"}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "might look like for our commonly"}, {"start": 580.0, "text": "used app architecture."}, {"start": 582.0, "text": "Let's talk about what a tabbed"}, {"start": 585.0, "text": "application might do like"}, {"start": 586.0, "text": "Safari."}, {"start": 587.0, "text": "You'll see that Safari here has"}, {"start": 588.0, "text": "two tabs open, each analogous to"}, {"start": 590.0, "text": "their own document."}, {"start": 592.0, "text": "And we should sort of think of"}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "each tab, since they're their"}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "own document, as having their"}, {"start": 596.0, "text": "own target content identifier."}, {"start": 598.0, "text": "But note, if we have two of"}, {"start": 600.0, "text": "these target content identifiers"}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "up on screen and we want to set"}, {"start": 603.0, "text": "it on our scene activation"}, {"start": 604.0, "text": "conditions as something we"}, {"start": 605.0, "text": "prefer, how would we do that?"}, {"start": 608.0, "text": "First, let's examine the canned"}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "predicate."}, {"start": 613.0, "text": "Simple enough."}, {"start": 615.0, "text": "Document-based apps can"}, {"start": 616.0, "text": "typically open any kind of"}, {"start": 617.0, "text": "documents in your application."}, {"start": 619.0, "text": "So to encode that, we actually"}, {"start": 621.0, "text": "use an always true predicate"}, {"start": 622.0, "text": "here to describe that any scene"}, {"start": 624.0, "text": "can display any content passed"}, {"start": 625.0, "text": "to it."}, {"start": 626.0, "text": "What kind of content does it"}, {"start": 627.0, "text": "prefer?"}, {"start": 628.0, "text": "Because this UI has multiple"}, {"start": 631.0, "text": "tabs, it makes sense that we'd"}, {"start": 632.0, "text": "use something like a compound"}, {"start": 633.0, "text": "predicate in order to gather all"}, {"start": 635.0, "text": "the subpredicates within it."}, {"start": 637.0, "text": "And then we'll use that with our"}, {"start": 639.0, "text": "scene activation conditions."}, {"start": 641.0, "text": "Great."}, {"start": 642.0, "text": "Well, for more information,"}, {"start": 644.0, "text": "please visit developer.apple.com."}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "We have all of our slides and"}, {"start": 647.0, "text": "notes and you can go there and"}, {"start": 648.0, "text": "get some more information about"}, {"start": 649.0, "text": "that."}, {"start": 650.0, "text": "And really, thank you for"}, {"start": 652.0, "text": "coming."}, {"start": 653.0, "text": "It has been a tremendous WWDC"}, {"start": 655.0, "text": "and we are so thrilled to see"}, {"start": 656.0, "text": "what you guys make with these"}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "new APIs."}]}
